    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (72.07) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.70) serving as our undisputed pillars. **Kyle Tucker** draws a favorable matchup against Phillips (xERA 4.52), where his efficiency is bolstered by a strong SP skill advantage. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-ceiling encounter with Bradish, where his park-adjusted metrics and favorable spot in the order make him our most reliable anchor. While **Jackson Merrill** (46.50) faces a tougher test against Perdomo, the wind blowing out at the venue provides a necessary 10% boost to his raw projection, keeping him in the lineup despite a sub-optimal platoon split. We are currently tracking \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Liam Hicks**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Drake Baldwin**; their final scores will fluctuate slightly once official cards are submitted, but their current projections suggest they hold enough intrinsic value to retain their starting spots.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (38.12) was the most difficult pivot of the day. While his raw base projection remains serviceable, the combination of a difficult matchup against Miles (xERA 3.20) and a negative platoon trend pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold for game-cap management. **Gunnar Henderson** (58.62) also draws Miles, but his elite offensive profile allows him to stay in the lineup despite the SP skill disadvantage that hindered **Coby Mayo**. We must remain vigilant regarding the health of our depth chart, as **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our ability to cycle in fresh legs if the weather or lineup conditions shift unexpectedly. As we push for those elusive stolen bases, we will continue to monitor the late-game efficiency of **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin** to ensure they maximize their utility as our primary table-setters.",
